  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b353-f848-cb7f-5404" name="Italian Hill Tribes (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #6 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The tribes of the central Italian highlands provided a tenacious foe for the lowland Latins. The Aequi and Volsci were dislodged into the lowlands by Samnite expansion in the fifth century BC and only beaten back near the end of the century. The Samnites themselves were only overcome after three wars lasting nearly fifty years from 343 BC to 295 BC. The Oscans moved down into the Campanian plain and overcame the Greek settlements there. Allies And Mercenaries: May have allied contingents from the Etruscan and Gallic lists, both at once if desired.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Italian Hill Tribes]
  Cavalry: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 40%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: up to 20% Infantry: At least 40% Skirmishers: up to 10% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
